  "criticalEvidence": [
    "Fade OnPlay26296 and LoopFade26322 share normalized opcodes except source name fade_/loopFade_ and loop false/true. Capture path/start/end/type/volume/setting/name; write End68 then Start64 then targetVolume48 before await. Await new/legacy clip. Native clip-null returns null, initial data-null calls Stop. Create/play source volume0, record clip.length56, invoke Fade(source,true,null) before returning source to base Play.",
    "Fade helper26289/26320 captures source, callback, direction, owner; only native-nonnull source schedules. Remove prior timer72 if nonzero, then assign SetCountDownByMillisecond(1000,complete,every). Each callback observes live targetVolume48 and fadeMilliseconds52. Every(id,remaining): in target*((float)duration-remaining)/duration, out target*(float)remaining/duration.",
    "Complete26299/26325 first RemoveTime(callback id). Destroyed captured source invokes optional callback and returns. Live fade-in sets target and returns without invoking optional callback. Fade-out sets0 then optional callback. Timer field is never reset, so completion plus Dispose can remove same id twice.",
    "OnStop26292/26316 first sets stopping60 true; for live source stores targetVolume=source.volume*GetSettingVolume again, then Fade(false,CompleteStop). Null source leaves stopping true and no timer/cleanup. Repeated Stop releases handle and Dispose directly without EndCall or flag reset.",
    "CompleteStop26290/26310 source.Stop -> EndCall -> handle.Release -> Dispose -> stopping=false. Exception ordering retained. OnDispose26286/26315 removes nonzero timer without clearing field, destroys source GameObject, clears source. Refresh26294/26314 writes live target on matching voice even without a source, then base writes native volume.",
    "Fade OnUpdate26293 and LoopFade26312 native source gate: if End<=0 evaluate isPlaying/time/length-fadeSeconds and require playing/time>=threshold/!stopping; else time>=End-fadeSeconds without stopping or playing gates. Fade calls OnStop. LoopFade marks stopping and fades out; callback26321 clears stopping and fades in, without seek or restart. Positive end repeats/resets countdown on each loop-fade update; Fade second update can direct-dispose without end.",
    "AudioCompositeBase26381 checks optional static override first then exact types1Once/2Loop/3Fade/4LoopFade/default null. Opcode ctor annotation for type3 aliases shared ctor6273; allocated usage3928512 resolves actual3408Fade. GetAudioType26382 missing config=>1 otherwise Ptype. Override return type verified from generic metadata reference6088."
  ],
